gth > 0\'. Ansible-lint might prefer using \'ansible.utils.conditionals\' for conditions, but since the user didn\'t mention changing functionality, I\'ll leave it as is unless it\'s causing an issue.\n\nNow, let me go through each task and make the necessary changes:\n\n1. For the import_tasks calls, I\'ll change them to use ansible.builtin.import_tasks.\n2. The apt module should be ansible.builtin.apt.\n3. The lineinfile module needs to be ansible.builtin.lineinfile.\n4. The meta module should be ansible.builtin.meta.\n5. Replace replace_content with ansible.builtin.replace.\n6. Fix the octal values by using 0o664.\n7. Ensure that all module names are correctly prefixed with their FQCN.\n\nI also notice that the \'notify\' parameter is causing warnings. Since it\'s a standard parameter for handlers, I\'ll leave it as is unless the linter marks it as fatal. If it\'s just a warning, it might be acceptable, but I should check if there\'s a better way. However, for now, I\'ll proceed without changing it.\n\nLet me structure each task with the corrected modules and parameters. I\'ll make sure each task uses the correct FQCN and that the octal values are properly formatted. Also, I\'ll replace replace_content with replace and adjust the parameters accordingly.\n\nAfter making these changes, I\'ll test the playbook with ansible-lint again to ensure all issues are resolved. This should make the playbook compliant without altering the intended functionality.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  ansible.builtin.import_tasks:\n    file: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Install required packages\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    name: "{{ grub_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Set GRUB_TIMEOUT\n  ansible.builtin.lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/default/grub\n    line: "GRUB_TIMEOUT={{ grub_timeout }}"\n    mode: 0o664\n    create: true\n    notify: Update grub\n\n- name: Set GRUB_RECORDFAIL_TIMEOUT\n  ansible.builtin.lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/default/grub\n    line: "GRUB_RECORDFAIL_TIMEOUT={{ grub_recordfail_timeout }}"\n    mode: 0o664\n    create: true\n    notify: Update grub\n\n- name: Add options to GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX\n  loop: "{{ grub_options }}"\n  ansible.builtin.replace:\n    path: /etc/default/grub\n    content: "GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX={{ item }}"\n    regex: \'^GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX=.*$\'\n    validate: \'/bin/sh -c "exit 0"\'\n    mode: 0o664\n    notify: Update grub\n  when: grub_options is defined and grub_options | length > 0\n\n- name: Import password.yml\n  ansible.builtin.import_tasks: password.yml\n  when: grub_set_password\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  ansible.builtin.meta:\n    flush_handlers: yes\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-16T16:46:34.744632493Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 26537963773, 'load_duration': 85127710, 'prompt_eval_count': 3439, 'prompt_eval_duration': 2154928573, 'eval_count': 1107, 'eval_duration': 24296241072, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--5b6bd306-f118-48b5-b3fb-ff637e631119-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3439, 'output_tokens': 1107, 'total_tokens': 4546}
