ectly structured.\n\nI also need to make sure that the `template` module\'s `dest` is set correctly, using `{{ item.name }}.conf` as the filename. The `notify` section should include both handlers, and the `file_mode` should be 0644.\n\nI should double-check the YAML syntax to ensure there are no errors. Each task should be a list under the main YAML document. I\'ll avoid any comments or explanations, as per the user\'s instructions.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll structure the playbook with \'---\' at the top, followed by the two tasks. Each task will have the required modules, parameters, and loops. I\'ll make sure that the variables are correctly referenced and that the playbook adheres to the specified structure for an Ansible Role.\n\nI think that\'s all. Now, I\'ll translate this into the YAML playbook as required.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create directories\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: "{{ directory.path }}"\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n  loop: "{{ httpd_directories }}"\n  loop_var: directory\n  register: directory_created\n\n- name: Configure directories\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: directory.conf.j2\n    dest: "{{ httpd_config_directory }}/{{ item.name }}.conf"\n    mode: 0644\n  loop: "{{ httpd_directories }}"\n  loop_var: item\n  notify: \n    - Test httpd configuration validity\n    - Restart httpd\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-16T18:05:36.660817111Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 15863710656, 'load_duration': 89708870, 'prompt_eval_count': 415, 'prompt_eval_duration': 130241942, 'eval_count': 784, 'eval_duration': 15642603080, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--5b206343-ca60-415c-8ad3-f103ac417196-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 415, 'output_tokens': 784, 'total_tokens': 1199}
