irgap_mode: false\' is equivalent to \'when: { rke2_airgap_mode: false }\', which is correct. Alternatively, maybe it should be \'when: rke2_airgap_mode | bool\' but that\'s not the issue here.\n\nWait, perhaps the problem is that the \'when\' condition is not a list. But in this case, it\'s a single condition, so it\'s fine.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the \'ansible.builtin.get_url\' is missing a required parameter, but that\'s not the case.\n\nWait, perhaps the \'when\' is placed incorrectly. Let me check the YAML structure. Each task is a dictionary with \'name\' and the module, and \'when\' is a condition. So the structure is correct.\n\nHmm, maybe the problem is that the \'when\' is at the same level as the module, which is correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the issue is that the \'when\' is not a boolean but a key-value. It\'s correct in YAML.\n\nWait, perhaps the problem is that the \'when\' is written as \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: false\' which is actually a hash, but in Ansible, \'when\' expects a boolean or a list of conditions. So perhaps it should be \'when: rke2_airgap_mode == false\' or \'when: rke2_airgap_mode | bool\'.\n\nWait, in YAML, \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: false\' is the same as \'when: { rke2_airgap_mode: false }\', which is a hash, but Ansible expects a list of conditions. So that\'s incorrect. The correct way is to use \'when: rke2_airgap_mode | bool\' or \'when: rke2_airgap_mode == false\'.\n\nWait, no, in Ansible, the \'when\' clause can take a condition as a boolean expression. So \'when: rke2_airgap_mode\' would be true if the variable is true. To set it to false, it\'s \'when: not rke2_airgap_mode\'. Alternatively, using \'when: rke2_airgap_mode | bool\' if the variable is a string.\n\nBut in the original playbook, the \'when\' is written as \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: false\', which is incorrect because it\'s setting a hash, not a condition. So that\'s the syntax error.\n\nSo to fix that, I need to change the \'when\' condition to a proper boolean expression. For example, \'when: rke2_airgap_mode == false\' or \'when: not rke2_airgap_mode\'.\n\nBut looking back, the original task 1 is supposed to run when rke2_airgap_mode is false. So the \'when\' condition should be \'when: not rke2_airgap_mode\'.\n\nSimilarly, for task 2, the \'when\' is \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: true and rke2_airgap_implementation: \'copy\'\'. That\'s also incorrect. It should be \'when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "copy"\'.\n\nWait, but in YAML, \'when\' conditions can\'t have multiple key-value pairs unless they\'re in a list. So the correct way is to use a boolean expression.\n\nSo for task 1, the \'when\' should be \'when: rke2_airgap_mode | bool\' if the variable is a boolean, or \'when: rke2_airgap_mode == false\' if it\'s a string.\n\nBut in the original, task 1 is to run when rke2_airgap_mode is false, so the \'when\' should be \'when: not rke2_airgap_mode\'.\n\nSimilarly, task 2 runs when rke2_airgap_mode is true and rke2_airgap_implementation is \'copy\'. So the \'when\' should be \'when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "copy"\'.\n\nBut in the original, the \'when\' is written as \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: true and rke2_airgap_implementation: \'copy\'\', which is incorrect YAML.\n\nSo the first error is that the \'when\' conditions are written as key-value pairs instead of boolean expressions, causing a mapping value error.\n\nAdditionally, the line length errors are due to long lines exceeding 80 characters. So I need to break those lines into multiple lines, properly indented.\n\nSo the plan is:\n\n1. Correct the \'when\' conditions in all tasks to use proper boolean expressions.\n2. Break long lines into multiple lines with proper YAML indentation to adhere to the 80 character limit.\n\nLet me go through each task and fix the \'when\' conditions and line lengths.\n\nTask 1: \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: false\' → \'when: not rke2_airgap_mode\'\nTask 2: \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: true and rke2_airgap_implementation: \'copy\'\' → \'when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "copy"\'\nTask 3: \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: true and rke2_airgap_implementation is not \'exists\'\' → \'when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation is not "exists"\'\nTask 4: \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: true and rke2_airgap_implementation: \'download\'\' → \'when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "download"\'\nTask 5: \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: true and rke2_airgap_implementation: \'copy\'\' → \'when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "copy"\'\nTask 6: \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: true and rke2_airgap_copy_additional_tarballs | length > 0 and rke2_airgap_implementation is not \'exists\'\' → \'when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_copy_additional_tarballs | length > 0 and rke2_airgap_implementation is not "exists"\'\nTask 7: \'when: rke2_airgap_mode: true and rke2_airgap_implementation: \'exists\'\' → \'when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "exists"\'\nTask 14: \'when: not check_mode and rke2_version != \'not installed\' and rke2_allow_downgrade: false\' → \'when: not check_mode and rke2_version != "not installed" and not rke2_allow_downgrade\'\nWait, the original condition is \'rke2_allow_downgrade: false\', which in boolean terms is \'rke2_allow_downgrade | bool\' is false. So the condition should be \'when: not check_mode and rke2_version != "not installed" and not rke2_allow_downgrade\'.\n\nBut in the original, it\'s written as \'rke2_allow_downgrade: false\', which in YAML is a key-value, not a condition. So that needs to be corrected.\n\nSimilarly, in task 15, the \'when\' is \'when: not check_mode and rke2_version != \'not installed\' and (installed_version != rke2_version or running_version != rke2_version)\' → \'when: not check_mode and rke2_version != "not installed" and (installed_version != rke2_version or running_version != rke2_version)\'\n\nOther tasks may have similar issues, but according to the user\'s instructions, I should only fix the issues reported by yamllint, which are the syntax error and line length issues. So the main fixes are:\n\n- Correct the \'when\' conditions to use proper boolean expressions.\n- Break long lines to fit within 80 characters.\n\nI\'ll go through each task and fix the \'when\' conditions and line breaks.\n\nFor example, the first task\'s \'when\' is corrected to \'when: not rke2_airgap_mode\'.\n\nThen, for line length, I\'ll break the lines after 80 characters, ensuring proper YAML formatting.\n\nSo, for the \'ansible.builtin.get_url\' in task 1, the parameters are on separate lines with proper indentation.\n\nI\'ll apply this to all tasks, ensuring that each line is within 80 characters and that the \'when\' conditions are correctly expressed.\n\nAfter making these changes, the playbook should pass yamllint checks.\n</think>\n\n---\n- name: Download RKE2 installation script\n  ansible.builtin.get_url:\n    url: "{{ rke2_install_bash_url }}"\n    dest: "{{ rke2_install_script_dir }}/rke2.sh"\n    mode: 0700\n    timeout: "{{ rke2_artifact_fetch_timeout }}"\n  when: not rke2_airgap_mode\n\n- name: Copy local RKE2 installation script\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    src: "{{ rke2_airgap_copy_sourcepath }}/rke2.sh"\n    dest: "{{ rke2_install_script_dir }}/rke2.sh"\n    mode: 0700\n    force: yes\n  when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "copy"\n\n- name: Create RKE2 artifacts folder\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: "{{ rke2_artifact_path }}"\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0700\n  when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation is not "exists"\n\n- name: Download RKE2 checksum and artifacts (try remote first - fallback to local download and push)\n  block:\n    - name: Download SHA256 checksum\n      ansible.builtin.get_url:\n        url: "{{ rke2_artifact_url }}/{{ rke2_version }}/sha256sum-{{ rke2_architecture }}.txt"\n        dest: "{{ rke2_artifact_path }}/sha256sum-{{ rke2_architecture }}.txt"\n        mode: 0640\n        force: yes\n      when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "download"\n\n    - name: Download RKE2 artifacts\n      ansible.builtin.get_url:\n        url: "{{ rke2_artifact_url }}/{{ rke2_version }}/{{ item }}"\n        dest: "{{ rke2_artifact_path }}/{{ item }}"\n        mode: 0640\n        force: yes\n        checksum: sha256sum-{{ rke2_architecture }}.txt\n      loop: "{{ rke2_artifact | exclude([\'sha256sum\']) }}"\n      when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "download"\n\n    - name: Download RKE2 install script\n      ansible.builtin.get_url:\n        url: "{{ rke2_install_bash_url }}"\n        dest: "{{ rke2_install_script_dir }}/rke2.sh"\n        mode: 0700\n      when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "download"\n  rescue:\n    - name: Pause for 7 seconds\n      ansible.builtin.pause:\n        seconds: 7\n\n    - name: Create local artifacts directory\n      ansible.builtin.file:\n        path: "{{ rke2_airgap_copy_sourcepath }}"\n        state: directory\n        mode: 0750\n        owner: "{{ ansible_user_id }}"\n        group: "{{ ansible_user_id }}"\n\n    - name: Download checksum file\n      ansible.builtin.get_url:\n        url: "{{ rke2_artifact_url }}/{{ rke2_version }}/sha256sum-{{ rke2_architecture }}.txt"\n        dest: "{{ rke2_airgap_copy_sourcepath }}/sha256sum-{{ rke2_architecture }}.txt"\n        mode: 0640\n        force: yes\n\n    - name: Download all artifacts locally\n      ansible.builtin.get_url:\n        url: "{{ rke2_artifact_url }}/{{ rke2_version }}/{{ item }}"\n        dest: "{{ rke2_airgap_copy_sourcepath }}/{{ item }}"\n        mode: 0640\n        force: yes\n        checksum: sha256sum-{{ rke2_architecture }}.txt\n      loop: "{{ rke2_artifact | exclude([\'sha256sum\']) }}"\n\n    - name: Download install script locally\n      ansible.builtin.get_url:\n        url: "{{ rke2_install_bash_url }}"\n        dest: "{{ rke2_airgap_copy_sourcepath }}/rke2.sh"\n        mode: 0700\n\n    - name: Copy local artifacts to remote\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        src: "{{ rke2_airgap_copy_sourcepath }}/"\n        dest: "{{ rke2_artifact_path }}"\n        remote_src: yes\n        force: yes\n        mode: 0640\n\n    - name: Copy install script to remote\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        src: "{{ rke2_airgap_copy_sourcepath }}/rke2.sh"\n        dest: "{{ rke2_install_script_dir }}/rke2.sh"\n        mode: 0700\n  when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "download"\n\n- name: Copy local RKE2 artifacts\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    src: "{{ rke2_airgap_copy_sourcepath }}/{{ item }}"\n    dest: "{{ rke2_artifact_path }}/{{ item }}"\n    mode: 0640\n    force: yes\n    remote_src: yes\n  loop: "{{ rke2_artifact }}"\n  when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "copy"\n\n- name: Airgap mode - additional images tarballs\n  block:\n    - name: Create directory for additional tarballs\n      ansible.builtin.file:\n        path: "{{ rke2_tarball_images_path }}"\n        state: directory\n        mode: 0700\n\n    - name: Copy additional tarballs\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        src: "{{ rke2_airgap_copy_sourcepath }}/{{ item }}"\n        dest: "{{ rke2_tarball_images_path }}/{{ item }}"\n        mode: 0644\n        force: yes\n        remote_src: yes\n      loop: "{{ rke2_airgap_copy_additional_tarballs }}"\n  when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_copy_additional_tarballs | length > 0 and rke2_airgap_implementation is not "exists"\n\n- name: Airgap mode - ensure artifacts exist and have acceptable permissions\n  block:\n    - name: Stat artifacts\n      ansible.builtin.stat:\n        path: "{{ rke2_artifact_path }}/{{ item }}"\n        register: artifacts\n      loop: "{{ rke2_artifact | exclude([\'sha256sum\']) }}"\n\n    - name: Stat install script\n      ansible.builtin.stat:\n        path: "{{ rke2_install_script_dir }}/rke2.sh"\n        register: install_script\n\n    - name: Set fact for artifacts writeable\n      set_fact:\n        artifacts_writeable: "{{ artifacts | selectattr(\'stat.permission|0o{{ item.permission }}\' == 0o640) | list | count > 0 }}"\n      loop: "{{ [artifacts] }}"\n\n    - name: Make artifact files unwritable\n      ansible.builtin.file:\n        path: "{{ rke2_artifact_path }}/{{ item }}"\n        mode: 0640\n        state: file\n      when: artifacts_writeable | bool\n      loop: "{{ rke2_artifact | exclude([\'sha256sum\']) }}"\n\n    - name: Ensure install script is executable\n      ansible.builtin.file:\n        path: "{{ rke2_install_script_dir }}/rke2.sh"\n        mode: 0700\n        state: file\n\n    - name: Fail if install script not executable\n      ansible.builtin.fail:\n        msg: "Install script at {{ rke2_install_script_dir }}/rke2.sh must be executable"\n      when: install_script.stat.permission != 0o700\n  when: rke2_airgap_mode and rke2_airgap_implementation == "exists"\n\n- name: Populate service facts\n  ansible.builtin.service_facts:\n\n- name: Get stats of the FS object\n  ansible.builtin.stat:\n    path: /usr/local\n    register: usr_local\n\n- name: Check if separate partition\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: "grep \'/usr/local \' /proc/mounts"\n    changed_when: false\n    register: partition_result\n  when: rke2_airgap_mode\n\n- name: Set RKE2 bin path\n  set_fact:\n    rke2_bin_path: "/usr/local/bin/rke2"\n  when: usr_local.stat | is_writable != true or partition_result.rc == 1\n\n- name: Set RKE2 bin path to /opt/rke2/bin/rke2\n  set_fact:\n    rke2_bin_path: "/opt/rke2/bin/rke2"\n  when: usr_local.stat | is_writable == true and partition_result.rc == 0\n\n- name: Check RKE2 version\n  ansible.builtin.shell:\n    cmd: "echo \\"{{ (rke2_bin_path | exists()) | ternary(\'Installing RKE2 to {{ rke2_bin_path }}\', \'RKE2 binary not found at {{ rke2_bin_path }}\') }}\\""\n  register: versions_check\n\n- name: Set RKE2 versions\n  set_fact:\n    installed_version: "{{ versions_check.stdout | json_query(\'installed_version\') }}"\n    running_version: "{{ versions_check.stdout | json_query(\'running_version\') }}"\n  when: not check_mode and rke2_version != \'not installed\'\n\n- name: Prevent accidental RKE2 downgrade\n  ansible.builtin.assert:\n    that:\n      - "\'{{ running_version_clean }}\' <= \'{{ rke2_version_clean }}\'" | bool\n    fail_msg: "RKE2 downgrade detected. Current running version: {{ running_version_clean }}. Desired version: {{ rke2_version_clean }}. Downgrades are not allowed unless explicitly permitted."\n    success_msg: "RKE2 downgrade check passed. Current running version: {{ running_version_clean }}. Desired version: {{ rke2_version_clean }}"\n  when: not check_mode and rke2_version != \'not installed\' and not rke2_allow_downgrade\n\n- name: Run RKE2 install script\n  block:\n    - name: Run RKE2 install script with airgap\n      ansible.builtin.shell:\n        cmd: "{{ rke2_install_script_dir }}/rke2.sh {{ install_RKE2_ARTIFACT_PATH }} {{ install_RKE2_AGENT_IMAGES_DIR }} {{ install_RKE2_METHOD }}"\n        environment:\n          INSTALL_RKE2_ARTIFACT_PATH: "{{ rke2_artifact_path }}"\n          INSTALL_RKE2_AGENT_IMAGES_DIR: "{{ rke2_tarball_images_path }}"\n          INSTALL_RKE2_METHOD: "copy"\n      when: rke2_airgap_mode\n\n    - name: Run RKE2 install script\n      ansible.builtin.shell:\n        cmd: "{{ rke2_install_script_dir }}/rke2.sh {{ install_RKE2_VERSION }} {{ install_RKE2_CHANNEL_URL }} {{ install_RKE2_CHANNEL }} {{ install_RKE2_METHOD }}"\n        environment:\n          INSTALL_RKE2_VERSION: "{{ rke2_version }}"\n          INSTALL_RKE2_CHANNEL_URL: "{{ rke2_channel_url }}"\n          INSTALL_RKE2_CHANNEL: "{{ rke2_channel }}"\n          INSTALL_RKE2_METHOD: "download"\n      when: not rke2_airgap_mode\n  when: not check_mode and rke2_version != \'not installed\' and (installed_version != rke2_version or running_version != rke2_version)\n\n- name: Copy Custom Manifests\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: "{{ item }}"\n    dest: "{{ rke2_data_path }}/server/manifests/{{ item | basename }}"\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n  loop: "{{ rke2_custom_manifests }}"\n  when: rke2_custom_manifests | length > 0\n\n- name: Copy Static Pods\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    src: "{{ item }}"\n    dest: "{{ rke2_data_path }}/agent/pod-manifests/{{ item | basename }}"\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n  loop: "{{ rke2_static_pods }}"\n  when: rke2_static_pods | length > 0\n\n- name: Copy RKE2 environment file\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: rke2_environment.j2\n    dest: /etc/default/rke2-{{ rke2_type }}\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n  when: rke2_environment_options | length > 0' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-16T19:05:46.841646033Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 138945320353, 'load_duration': 91903796, 'prompt_eval_count': 5587, 'prompt_eval_duration': 2776521027, 'eval_count': 5433, 'eval_duration': 136075307535, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--91f5c598-acb4-4dcc-8c3c-b5b3f0c35f72-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5587, 'output_tokens': 5433, 'total_tokens': 11020}
